            <div xml:id="d602">

                <pb facs="0796" n="706" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg706"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.113 (Manchuria) Petroleum/47: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-10T12:00:00+08:00">April 10,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 10—7:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>160. Department’s 85, March 30, 6 p.m. British Legation has had nothing from its
                    Foreign Office. American Consul General at Mukden<anchor n="87" xml:id="d602-f1"
                    /> reports however that his British colleague informed him that advices from his
                    Embassy [at] Tokyo indicate British Embassy proposes to make similar
                    representations in line with our suggestion. Myers expresses belief that similar
                    representations by American Embassy had become desirable.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d602-f1" n="87" xml:id="d602-f1-content">
